  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2018;Reaching the Unreached&#x2019;- Ensuring universal access to TB prevention and care services for all - India (01-Jan-2018-31-Mar-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India, Tuberculosis, International Union Against Tuberculosis and Lung Disease (The Union)This program has the following goals: To achieve a rapid decining burden of TB morbidity and mortality while working towards elimination of TB in India by 2025. The objectives of this program are: Early detection of TB cases by Active Case finding in targeted groups and initiate treatment promptly.  Systematically engage the private provides  with an increase in case notification to 2 million cases annually.  Improving treatment adherence and treatment support byadoption of iCT tools and partnerships.  Strengthen linkages with the Pharmacovigilance program of india ( PvPI) for monitoring, identification and detection of signals..  Health system strengthening with focus on mechanisms for critical mangement reforms, restructuring HR and Financial norms..  Promote Research on issues which are the key relevance to guide interventions and to monitor and evaluate the impact of the program through collaboration with specialized institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
